WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.611 --> 00:00:16.692
knew she had made a big mistake at school.

2
00:00:17.873 --> 00:00:21.115
She should have let Joy tell the big news about the chickens.

3
00:00:21.135 --> 00:00:27.298
"I need some exciting news of my own," thought Katie as she finished setting the table.

4
00:00:27.318 --> 00:00:32.056
"Something bigger than bangs."

5
00:00:32.076 --> 00:00:33.957
"Suppertime!" called Grandpa.

6
00:00:33.977 --> 00:00:36.338
"My famous spaghetti and meatballs."

7
00:00:37.538 --> 00:00:41.680
The family sat down at the kitchen table, and Mom started filling plates.

8
00:00:43.421 --> 00:00:44.981
Joy shot a look at Katie.

9
00:00:45.001 --> 00:00:49.843
"Everyone asked me a million questions about the baby chickens today.

10
00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:51.404
And Mr.

11
00:00:51.464 --> 00:00:54.305
Higgins asked me to bring some chicks to school in a few weeks!"

12
00:00:55.846 --> 00:00:57.766
Katie felt her face turn red.

13
00:00:57.786 --> 00:01:01.428
"Luke brought an earthworm to school," she said quickly.

14
00:01:02.588 --> 00:01:04.589
"It was 23 centimeters long."

15
00:01:04.609 --> 00:01:06.611
"Oh my!"

16
00:01:07.191 --> 00:01:08.112
exclaimed Mom.

17
00:01:08.132 --> 00:01:11.734
"I don't like worms," said Joy.

18
00:01:11.754 --> 00:01:13.055
"They're yucky."

19
00:01:13.075 --> 00:01:16.978
"I think worms are cool," explained Katie.

20
00:01:16.998 --> 00:01:20.600
"Maybe we should all sell worms too!"

21
00:01:21.821 --> 00:01:23.322
suggested Dad, laughing.

22
00:01:23.342 --> 00:01:26.904
"Not me," said Joy with a shiver.

23
00:01:26.924 --> 00:01:32.348
"I brought home a sturdy cardboard box from the recycling center today," said Dad.

24
00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.161
"It will make a good house for the chicks."

25
00:01:36.823 --> 00:01:40.746
"I bought chicken feed and some other stuff at the store today," said Grandpa.

26
00:01:40.766 --> 00:01:43.448
"Everything is in the spare room."

27
00:01:44.649 --> 00:01:46.830
Katie suddenly jumped up from her chair.

28
00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:49.833
"Aha!" she exclaimed.

29
00:01:49.853 --> 00:01:51.134
"I got it!"

30
00:01:51.634 --> 00:01:52.695
Everyone stared at her.

31
00:01:52.715 --> 00:01:55.617
"What?" asked Mom.

32
00:01:55.637 --> 00:01:59.160
"I'm going to help Luke sell worms!"

33
00:02:00.352 --> 00:02:03.754
Katie dashed out of the kitchen and up the stairs to her room.

34
00:02:04.895 --> 00:02:09.357
"That child is full of surprises," said Mom, shaking her head.

35
00:02:10.498 --> 00:02:11.898
Joy didn't say anything.

36
00:02:13.119 --> 00:02:17.421
She was still a little mad at Katie for blurting out the news about the chicks.

37
00:02:19.022 --> 00:02:20.343
"Well, what are we waiting for?"

38
00:02:20.823 --> 00:02:21.423
asked Dad.

39
00:02:21.444 --> 00:02:24.345
"The chicks should arrive in the mail tomorrow.

40
00:02:24.745 --> 00:02:25.546
Let's get to work!"

41
00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:29.248
They all headed upstairs to the spare room.

42
00:02:30.428 --> 00:02:33.351
The supplies Grandpa had bought were piled on the floor.

43
00:02:34.492 --> 00:02:38.835
Dad cleared off a table and set his big cardboard box on top.

44
00:02:38.855 --> 00:02:43.399
"A chick house is called a brooder," explained Mom.

45
00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:49.484
She was sitting on the bed, reading from her library book How to Raise Chickens.

46
00:02:50.625 --> 00:02:54.329
"We need to put holes in the sides so air can flow through the box."

47
00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:57.732
"I can do that," replied Dad.

48
00:02:58.908 --> 00:03:02.251
Joy picked up some shopping bags and opened them on the bed.

49
00:03:02.271 --> 00:03:04.513
"Look at this stuff!"

50
00:03:05.013 --> 00:03:06.014
she cried happily.

51
00:03:06.034 --> 00:03:07.735
"Here's the chicken feeder!

52
00:03:08.295 --> 00:03:09.396
And a water jar!"

53
00:03:09.416 --> 00:03:13.339
"Here's the heat lamp," said Grandpa.

54
00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:18.763
"The lamp should be about half a meter above the chicks," explained Mom.

55
00:03:18.783 --> 00:03:21.686
"The babies need to be kept warm."

56
00:03:22.286 --> 00:03:24.308
Grandpa clamped the lamp on the box.

57
00:03:25.988 --> 00:03:28.910
Joy emptied a bag of wood shavings into the box.

58
00:03:30.211 --> 00:03:34.274
As she spread them out, Grandpa filled the feeder and the water jar.

59
00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:38.897
He put them in the box, and Mom added a thermometer.

60
00:03:38.917 --> 00:03:41.859
"Ready?" asked Mom.

61
00:03:41.879 --> 00:03:44.781
"Ready!" cried Joy.

62
00:03:46.262 --> 00:03:50.445
Suddenly something flew through the air and landed right in the brooder!

63
00:03:50.465 --> 00:03:52.727
"Oh, Jellybean!"

64
00:03:53.227 --> 00:03:54.028
cried Joy.

65
00:03:55.312 --> 00:03:59.676
She put her arms around Jellybean's belly and lifted her out of the box.

66
00:04:01.658 --> 00:04:03.139
Jellybean screeched.

67
00:04:03.159 --> 00:04:05.160
"Go away!"

68
00:04:05.781 --> 00:04:06.622
scolded Joy.

69
00:04:06.642 --> 00:04:08.323
"No cats allowed!"

70
00:04:09.544 --> 00:04:12.567
Jellybean ran down the hallway to the twins' bedroom.

71
00:04:13.668 --> 00:04:15.529
Katie was talking on the telephone.

72
00:04:15.549 --> 00:04:18.652
"Okay, Luke," she said.

73
00:04:18.672 --> 00:04:19.893
"Tomorrow night.

74
00:04:20.353 --> 00:04:23.556
A flashlight a bucket a rag.

75
00:04:24.732 --> 00:04:26.335
I'll have everything ready.

76
00:04:26.755 --> 00:04:27.616
Thanks, partner!"

77
00:04:28.137 --> 00:04:29.218
She hung up the phone.

78
00:04:29.239 --> 00:04:31.822
"Big news, Jellybean!"

79
00:04:32.403 --> 00:04:33.504
said Katie happily.

80
00:04:33.524 --> 00:04:35.808
"I'm in the bait business!"
